  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 249 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nA stationary front hangs out over the northern part of our CWA\nfor most of the week and brings off and on rain chances for\ncentral MO. High pressure will sit over southern MO and keep\nthat area mostly dry through mid-week. Once that ridge begins \nto move east later in the week, rain chances become more\nwidespread by the end of the week. Unfortunately, not a lot of \ntemperature changes or any signs of a cooldown coming this week.\nIn fact, there may need to be Heat Advisories issued this week\nwith the prolonged heat indices near 105 degrees especially for\nareas south of I-44. High temperatures drop into the 80s for\nnext weekend.",
